{
  "title": "Work and school",
  "note": "Tener que + infinitive means to have to: Tengo que estudiar. Saber is to know facts or how to do something (sé, sabes, sabe); conocer is to know a person or place (conozco, conoces, conoce), with a before a person: Conozco a Ana. Computer is la computadora in Latin America and el ordenador in Spain.",
  "src": {"t": "Spanish 1A: Beginning Spanish (LibreTexts)", "u": "https://human.libretexts.org/Courses/Chabot_College/Spanish_1A%3A_Beginning_Spanish_(2026)"},
